Wojciech,

This looks great!

I would just add that I had casually been working on a related project over the past few weeks to expose some JavaScript libraries to R, starting with Protovis: http://code.google.com/p/rwebvis/. I'm about ready to release an early version of this, after which point I would love to open it up. I think that there are many opportunities for good web graphics from these JavaScript and Ajax frameworks, including interactivity and animation.

On a related point: there are many R graphics packages at this point. It might be worth creating an abstract framework for more sophisticated graphical packages, in the vein that DBI provides for database packages?  This could greatly ease adoption for new users.

Thanks,
Shane

