Maybe R-forge? Starting a list per project may be overkill, but does give
student/mentor/others an archived correspondence resource at little
overhead, in addition to SVN and check/build services if the project is a
package? I can't see myself remembering to look at a blog ever, doesn't
happen, I'm afraid (an age thing, no doubt, even with RSS). But students &
mentors could lurk on each others' lists, couldn't they, possibly
digested? Using the commit list probably isn't a good idea, though ...

